course: dictionary
lesson: 13802
title: Calling for help: the word invocation
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: An invocation is a call. When you invoke something, you call on it for help, blessing or authority. Look at the clues around the word: the sentence will talk about asking, calling out or praying, and often something important is being called on. «The service began with an invocation, a short prayer asking for God's blessing.» The clue is prayer, so an invocation is a prayer asking for help.
explain: Invocation is a noun, and its verb is invoke. You can see the same root in both. «The lawyer's invocation of the old rule saved her client.» Here the lawyer called on a rule as her authority. Ask yourself: what is being called on, and why? That question unlocks most meanings of this word.
explain: Stories use the word too. «The wizard began his invocation, and a cold wind swept the room as the spirit rose.» The wizard is calling up a spirit with words, which is a magic spell. Once you read the clues, the meaning is clear, even if the word looks long and strange.
fact: Invocation means a call for help, blessing or authority.
fact: In church, an invocation is a prayer at the start of a service, asking for blessing.
fact: In law, to invoke a rule is to call on it as your authority.
fact: In magic stories, an invocation is a spell that calls up a spirit.
fact: Old poems often begin with an invocation to the Muse, a call for inspiration.
exercise: «The service began with an invocation, a prayer for blessing.» What is an invocation here? | A song of thanks sung at the end | A list of the people who came | *A prayer asking for help or blessing | A loud shout of joy
exercise: «The judge accepted her invocation of an old law.» What does invoking a law mean? | Breaking the law on purpose | Writing a new law from scratch | *Calling on the law as your authority | Forgetting the law completely
exercise: «The wizard's invocation made the spirit appear.» In this story, what is an invocation? | A map showing the way to a castle | A kind of cake eaten at feasts | *A spell said to call up a spirit | A gentle breeze on a hot day
test: Which word is the verb linked to invocation, meaning to call on something for help? | invent | ignore | inform | *invoke
test: Which sentence uses invocation to mean a magic spell? | «The choir sang an invocation for the harvest.» | «The invocation of the rule saved the case.» | «The invocation was a long list of names.» | *«The wizard's invocation made a spirit rise from the floor.»
exam: «The priest began with an invocation, asking God to bless the room.» What is an invocation? | A rule that a court must follow | A sudden noise in the church | *A prayer asking for help or blessing | A magic potion that makes you invisible
